invariant: INV-16
file: p256_wide_point.c
catches: diff_p256_wide
reason: the incomplete addition adds vvv * Y1 to Y3 where the formula
  takes it away, so Y3 comes out for another point. bin/diff_p256_wide
  holds the steps to spec/lean/Spec/P256WidePoint.lean's
  addAffineIncomplete, coordinate for coordinate, which is what makes the
  Lean proof that the steps add two points a proof about this file.

--- old
    p256_wide_fe_mul(&t, &vvv, &a->y);
    p256_wide_fe_sub(&y3, &y3, &t);
--- new
    p256_wide_fe_mul(&t, &vvv, &a->y);
    p256_wide_fe_add(&y3, &y3, &t);
